# USDA FoodData Central key — free: https://fdc.nal.usda.gov/api-key-signup.html
# Copy to .env (gitignored). This is an Edge Function secret: `food-search`
# reads it server-side and the client never sees it. Keep it private — USDA
# deactivates published keys — and never expose it to the app, which is why the
# whole FDC fan-out runs in the function rather than on the device.
FDC_API_KEY=

# Supabase, for the app. Both are the opposite case to the key above: they are
# *designed* to ship inside the client build, and auth and RLS protect the data
# rather than the secrecy of these strings. Copy the real values from Project
# Settings → API Keys; use the publishable key (`sb_publishable_…`), not the
# legacy anon JWT, which is compatibility-only.
#
# The EXPO_PUBLIC_ prefix outlived Expo. apps/ios/Scripts/write-config.sh reads
# these names into the iOS build, and renaming them means changing the script,
# project.yml, AppConfiguration and the UI tests together.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
